  "source_logic_review": {
    "paired_statistic": "Each block contrast is DeltaP minus DeltaE with both terms from the same frozen fitted arms; empty and final blocks retained.",
    "bootstrap": "Within each fold, draw n blocks independently with replacement, sum their uncentered paired contrasts, then sum independent fold draws for pooled intervals. Percentiles 0.025 and0.975; 49999 draws.",
    "permutation": "Independently multiply each paired block contrast by +/-1, compare absolute total to observed absolute total, use add-one numerator and denominator. This is a symmetry-based paired block sign-flip randomization procedure, not a refitted likelihood-ratio calibration.",
    "sign_test": "Two-sided binomial test of block signs after excluding absolute contrasts <=1e-12; it ignores contrast magnitude and can disagree with the sign-flip statistic.",
    "terminal_block": "Last block is shorter and receives the same resampling probability as every full block; the implemented conditional block procedure retains it without duration reweighting.",
    "pooling": "Chronological test folds are disjoint and contiguous within each catalogue. Bootstrap resamples separately within folds. It does not pool NZ and California."
  },
  "interpretation": {
